{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773594153,"nonce":"/aZn/XfuxnXTMX1g7SmADmlcW3U=","title":"Merge latest base branch into agent worktree at every transition point","message":"When master advances while the agent is working, the agent can revert those changes when its branch is merged back. The agent should be told to revise its work by merging the latest master at every transition point.\n\n## Current state\n\n- Fresh start: branches from latest master — OK\n- Resume (orphan/context-limit): merge_base_into_worktree added (7bb505f) but on conflict it aborts silently — agent is NOT told to merge\n- Pre-review rebase: exists in core/rebase.py, handles conflicts by resuming agent — OK\n- Accept merge: host/merge.py does merge --no-ff with rebase fallback — no pre-check for divergence\n\n## Required behavior\n\nAt every transition point where master may have changed, the host should:\n1. Fetch latest base branch into the worktree\n2. Attempt merge of base into agent branch\n3. If clean merge: proceed normally\n4. If conflicts: abort merge, but write a merge-needed.txt to the session dir with conflict details and the merge target\n5. Container entrypoint: on resume, if merge-needed.txt exists, prepend instructions to the agent prompt telling it to merge the latest base branch, resolve conflicts, run tests, then continue its work\n\n## Pathways to cover\n\n1. Resume (orphan restart): watcher detects orphan -\u003e merge_base_into_worktree -\u003e if conflicts, write merge-needed.txt -\u003e container starts with merge instructions in prompt\n2. Resume (context limit): SessionRunner auto-resumes within container — no host merge happens, but pre-review rebase catches it at the end\n3. Resume (manual nightshift resume): same as orphan — host-side merge before container start\n4. Pre-review (@@DONE@@): already handled by core/rebase.py — keep as-is\n5. Accept: before merging into master, verify agent branch is not behind base — if it is, reject the accept and tell user to resume first\n\n## Tests needed\n\n- merge_base_into_worktree: clean merge preserves master changes in worktree\n- merge_base_into_worktree: conflicting merge writes merge-needed.txt with details\n- merge_base_into_worktree: no-op when base has not advanced (no divergence)\n- entrypoint: merge-needed.txt content is prepended to resume prompt\n- entrypoint: merge-needed.txt is cleaned up after being consumed\n- accept: rejects if agent branch is behind base (integration test)\n- full cycle: start -\u003e master advances -\u003e resume -\u003e agent sees merge instructions\n- full cycle: start -\u003e master advances -\u003e done -\u003e pre-review rebase catches divergence\n\n## Files to modify\n\n- host/workspace_setup.py: merge_base_into_worktree returns status, writes merge-needed.txt on conflict\n- entrypoint.py: read merge-needed.txt on resume, prepend to prompt\n- host/cli.py (cmd_accept): check if agent branch is behind base before merging\n- tests/test_workspace_setup.py (new): tests for merge_base_into_worktree\n- tests/test_launch.py: test merge-needed.txt flow\n- tests/test_accept_reject.py: test accept-behind-base rejection\n\nREQ-001, REQ-006","files":null}]}